<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zmitser Zhylunovich</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1887">1887</a>–<a href="/years/1937">1937</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Tsishka Hartny</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zmitser Zhylunovich was a Belarusian writer, known by the pen name Tsishka Hartny, and head of the provisional government of the Socialist Soviet Republic of Byelorussia proclaimed in January 1919. He broke with the Bolsheviks when the republic was merged into the Lithuanian-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byelorussian-ssr">Byelorussian SSR</a>, and later worked as a writer and editor. He died during the purges in 1937.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zmitser-zhylunovich.jpg" alt="Zmitser Zhylunovich" width="192" height="295" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%A6%D1%96%D1%88%D0%BA%D0%B0_%D0%93%D0%B0%D1%80%D1%82%D0%BD%D1%8B.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
